```mdl
verdict SyncDiscordChannel: Pull-only sync works per binding, but it runs two at once and fails the operation when any binding fails.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-discord/src/types/DiscordOperation.ts#SyncDiscordChannel, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-discord/src/operations/sync.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-connector/src/Binding.ts#syncAll]
  walkthrough:
    - The operation declares the connection and priority input and the pulled output. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-discord/src/types/DiscordOperation.ts#SyncDiscordChannel
    - syncAll fans out over the connection's cursors and surfaces the worst failure at the end. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-connector/src/Binding.ts#syncAll
    - The per-binding sync pages messages after the cursor, maps them, appends to the feed and toasts. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-discord/src/operations/sync.ts
  note: |
    `SYNC_CONCURRENCY` is 2, not 3. After all bindings run, `syncAll` re-fails the operation with the first binding
    failure, so the operation fails on one bad target, which the spec says it should not. No test runs the operation.
```

